---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Principles"
  description="The architecture principles behind the generated Astro and Hayate profile."
>
  <main class="principles-page">
    <p class="section-label">System principles</p>
    <h1>One contract.<br />Two moments.</h1>
    <div class="principle-list">
      <section>
        <span>Build</span>
        <h2>Public is durable.</h2>
        <p>
          Local editorial data becomes static HTML. A build never receives a
          reader cookie and never snapshots identity-scoped Hayate responses.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>Browse</span>
        <h2>Private is timely.</h2>
        <p>
          The visible island hydrates in the browser and sends same-origin
          credentials directly to Hayate.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>Extend</span>
        <h2>SSR is a choice.</h2>
        <p>
          Add an official adapter only when a BFF is genuinely needed. Keep
          domain logic, validation, and storage in Hayate.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <a class="return-link" href="/">Return to field notes →</a>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
